ers of the Week (in the &quot;to hate&quot; fashion-I think I'm going to stay up for a week after Nibbles the Face Jester's episode). Also praying for the return of Jersey after they explained he can come back after banishment, brah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hear they're going to introduce upgrades to Stars like they did with Luna and Night, make his powers more reliable at the cost of being less controllable. Think they're going to introduce that new Ranger, Patchwork, before getting to the Candlelight Brigade and Morticia. You can already see it in how Centaur's growing desperation is being played up, what with how Dr. Mongol is progressing from &quot;improve humanity at all costs&quot; to &quot;humanity is a weakness.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T17:15:42-08:00","id":798030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=797527#post797527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Decided to revive this in honor of the new season. Love the new Monsters of the Week (in the &quot;to hate&quot; fashion-I think I'm going to stay up for a week after Nibbles the Face Jester's episode). Also praying for the return of Jersey after they explained he can come back after banishment, brah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hear they're going to introduce upgrades to Stars like they did with Luna and Night, make his powers more reliable at the cost of being less controllable. Think they're going to introduce that new Ranger, Patchwork, before getting to the Candlelight Brigade and Morticia. You can already see it in how Centaur's growing desperation is being played up, what with how Dr. Mongol is progressing from &quot;improve humanity at all costs&quot; to &quot;humanity is a weakness.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally felt really sorry for the KIBs. Poor dears just wanted to go home, but scared everyone away. Though the Mexican standoff between the Rangers, the KIBs' parents, their kidnappers, the group of conspiracy theorists and the MIB internal affairs squad was golden. But then, I've always been a sucker for a good Mexican standoff.<br /> <br /> Also, I've heard rumors that the writers are considering having one of the Candlelight Brigade members turn evil, you know, the rich one from the Hell Fire Club? Seems their considering having him join the Most Dangerous Game Society. Personally I would rather they retooled the Hell Fire club to make more clear that were about messing with monsters socially. And have the group clean house and get rid of the creepy overtones of some of the groups members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T21:18:34-08:00","id":811534,"title":"","content":"Did anyone else catch that recent mini-episode, the one that aired right after Ranger Perdition's alternate universe adventure? It showed things from the Geas of Heaven's perspective and the whole thing makes me wonder if the other two Geas factions would even be hunting Selina's followers if it weren't for the Silver-Haired Father's followers egging that on.<br /> <br /> And speaking of the Ivory Royals in that episode, HOLY SHIT! is it just me or did the content of that phone call between the Ivory Princess and that priest of the Cult of the Mad Wolf imply that the Ivory Prince knocked up Christina during the party after they teamed up to kill the Mockery Hunter King? If that is the case, wouldn't that make him a target of his family's hunts, seeing as how they hunt those that dishonor their families?<br /> <br /> Me thinks things are about to get interesting with our favorite werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:30:36-08:00","id":1033896,"title":"","content":"Whoa...We are getting a reboot movie!<br /> Apparently some of the newer stuff still counts, but we haven't seen two ofthe 'old style' rangers yet. Seriously, Ranger Dream hasn't shown up since the Cosmic Device reformatted causality.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I am loving the new line up.Ranger Perdition and Ranger Devoured have lovely snide snarky dialogue and the irony that Perdition has such a hate on her because of the CD sees her and her family as a threat, so he doesn't actually WANT to hate her...Plus Adam finding another of his kind and passing on the mantle of Ranger Storm was kind of touching...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:19:25-08:00","id":1033990,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly interested in seeing the Renegade Rangers, though. They look like they're going to be an interesting wrinkle to throw at some of the Rangers' worldviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:58:32-08:00","id":1034417,"title":"","content":"Can I lodge a minor complaint here?<br /> <br /> I know they were going for &quot;eldritch&quot; with the Eyeless Devourer's true form to contrast with how surprisingly human Ranger Nightmare looks, but did they have to include so many fractals? My eyes started to hurt a bit looking at him.<br /> <br /> And uh, the belly-egg thing. Ew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T20:55:15-08:00","id":1034436,"title":"","content":"I'm more interested in talking about Steve's last focus arc , &quot;the covenant pentology&quot;, I can't help but think it's mostly a &quot;ground-work&quot; episode, something meant to set up even more awesome stuff for Steve later, but finally learning whether or not that scary catholic vampire survived Katrina was pretty good and it's obvious that that one scene in the episode focuses on the Bloody Mother's Chorus is meant to set up that episode on Steve's renfield and the other not-quite vamps that I mentioned a while back, though I seem to be missing the all those clues on the identity of the Unknown Tyrannt in Canada that people keep claiming are in the episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T18:47:05-07:00","id":1235765,"title":"","content":"Another year, another season. Good to see that Netflix's audience knows good animation when they see it. Hear they actually made a continuance of the original series, anyone got a bead on that?<br /> <br /> So, they're really leaning on the fact that Morticia tied to ghosts this season, going by the teasers. Also, Void seems to be his own character again, which is awesome, though he seems to be more of a Berserk But Fundamentally Noble Protector kind of superpowered evil side this time around (anyone see him break down and beg Morticia for forgiveness after he had to drain one of Chris' trees and let out Wolf Foe to save her? Heartbreaking).<br /> <br /> Also, holy shit, the Wardens of Woe are freaking scary. Using the armor of fallen Rangers, Jesus; it's like they're taunting their prey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T22:13:45-07:00","id":1235811,"title":"","content":"Tell me about it. Seriously tell me. I was distracted by the Deep One Ghost knockoffs and the idea that Mortia's fellow Returned are literally invader the Deadlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T22:44:34-07:00","id":1235815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1235765#post1235765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, holy shit, the Wardens of Woe are freaking scary. Using the armor of fallen Rangers, Jesus; it's like they're taunting their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little more concerned with how much of a sellout Ranger Conquest is, personally, but you can't deny the Vale of Tears and the Mortal Coils have teeth to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T23:54:51-07:00","id":1235822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1235815#post1235815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little more concerned with how much of a sellout Ranger Conquest is, personally, but you can't deny the Vale of Tears and the Mortal Coils have teeth to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, seriously on Conquest. I didn't think much about Deaf Simon until he fucking put <i>Void</i> under heel. It's the kind of thing that brings to vibe the sort of enemies that pop up in Amon- and Ranger Stars-centric episodes, albeit with more....of a shot, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:28:52-07:00","id":1236112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1235822#post1235822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, seriously on Conquest. I didn't think much about Deaf Simon until he fucking put <i>Void</i> under heel. It's the kind of thing that brings to vibe the sort of enemies that pop up in Amon- and Ranger Stars-centric episodes, albeit with more....of a shot, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Simon's seriously unnerving. It's like Series One Void (and I just noticed they switched pronouns, makes me think of Void as his own thing), except while you could always tell what Ranger Void wanted (hurting her other half in some way, and reveling in how much the team needed her at times despite her cheerfully stating how much she enjoyed toying with them), Conquest has his own agenda. I saw a couple SFX similar to how Eclispe calls on her ghost attacks, which leads me to think he has his own Void too, but given how he mocked Morticia for not &quot;training&quot; Void properly, I get the sense he's something way worse. <br /> <br /> And yeah, given what the Wardens regard as a crime, I'm considering them not the most reliable narrators on who the bad guy is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:23:49-07:00","id":1236510,"title":"","content":"OOC: Is anyone else getting a Rooster Teeth vibe from this? I can imagine the Nomad of Nowhere happily wandering in and nobody realizing he's from a different continuity. Cue crossover with the baddies and Toth's crew trying to one-up each other to get him and his animation powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:43:27-07:00","id":1236631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1236510#post1236510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOC: Is anyone else getting a Rooster Teeth vibe from this? I can imagine the Nomad of Nowhere happily wandering in and nobody realizing he's from a different continuity. Cue crossover with the baddies and Toth's crew trying to one-up each other to get him and his animation powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T21:28:25-07:00","id":1236670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1236631#post1236631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it only makes sense if you're familiar with how gleefully Rooster Teeth hosts shows that seem like light comedy and suddenly turn into dramatic epics with light comedy-style characters. Red Vs. Blue, anyone?<br /> <br /> Darkness Rangers seems like something similar, high-action funny Power Rangers stuff mixed in with seriously dark villains not afraid to turn to mind games to break their adversaries.<br /> <br /> IC:<br /> <br /> Actually, something I just noticed;<br /> <br /> You know how each of the BBEG factions have their own instrument in their leitmotif? The Stolos Shadows their violin, the Lunatic Exiles their theremin, the Stormchasers their synthesizers. With the Wardens, their instrumentation is trumpets, same as Morticia's theme. Nice touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T21:32:51-07:00","id":1236671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1236670#post1236670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, it only makes sense if you're familiar with how gleefully Rooster Teeth hosts shows that seem like light comedy and suddenly turn into dramatic epics with light comedy-style characters. Red Vs. Blue, anyone?<br /> <br /> Darkness Rangers seems like something similar, high-action funny Power Rangers stuff mixed in with seriously dark villains not afraid to turn to mind games to break their adversaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still OOC Here: I had not <i>quite</i> realized that connection till now, which is funny due to just how god damn much Rooster Teeth I watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:29:01-07:00","id":1236822,"title":"","content":"I hate to be that guy, but i am totally lost on who is who","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:22:54-07:00","id":1236855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1236822#post1236822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to be that guy, but i am totally lost on who is who</div> </div> </div> </div>OOC: The ones I came up with were:<br /> <br /> Stolos Shadows: Strix<br /> <br /> Lunatic Exiles: Idigam<br /> <br /> Stormchasers: Alchemists (because Ranger Storm is a Promethean)<br /> <br /> Wardens of Woe: Reapers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:24:40-07:00","id":1236857,"title":"","content":"Deaf Simon, aka Ranger Conquest is whatever the hell we call Bound who have Tyranny instead of Synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:30:34-07:00","id":1236860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1236822#post1236822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to be that guy, but i am totally lost on who is who</div> </div> </div> </div>Morticia is the Sin-Eater of this fictional series. Ranger Void/Umbra is her geist.<br /> <br /> Deaf Simon/<s>Ranger</s> Rider Conquest is a stand-in for Bound who've changed their Synergy rating to Tyranny by destroying their geist's Touchstone \u2014 we haven't seen the mechanics for them yet, but there's a strong candidate for an example in <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2237275\" target=\"_blank\">one of the fiction previews</a>.<br /> <br /> The Wardens of Woe are Reapers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T23:49:36-07:00","id":1253223,"title":"","content":"What, no love for the Psycho Rangers in Neo? (I missed the original series, so I can't comment on that, would like to hear how well they worked.)<br /> <br /> I thought they were all pretty well set up, introducing them individually before the massive team battles. Sure the conflicting agendas were a little predictable, but what's a Psycho Rangers story without a teamwork aesop? And the show runners sure pulled out all the stops making the episodes suitably epic. Especially when Psycho Ranger Abyss and Psycho Rangers Bale and Brood inevitably came to blows. Evil and Oblivion just can't get along. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:03:47-07:00","id":1256974,"title":"","content":"I don't know guys, i feel like the monster hunters are the best characters, I mean sure they're just human, have no powers to speak of, and well get very little screen time compared to the psycho rangers, but their characters and determination are nothing to sneeze at. I honestly think that their a very under-used part of the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24642-mr-perfect-cell","name":"Mr.Perfect cell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:14:15-07:00","id":1313328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Perfect cell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1256974#post1256974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know guys, i feel like the monster hunters are the best characters, I mean sure they're just human, have no powers to speak of, and well get very little screen time compared to the psycho rangers, but their characters and determination are nothing to sneeze at. I honestly think that their a very under-used part of the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I hear there was a bit of a scheduling kerfuffle; they wanted Morticia's arc to be before theirs, for whatever reason. Also, the Tsarina Pestis arc and its...rather mind-screwy antagonists. Nice touch that they called out Sterliza for being just as much of a monster as the Psychos for her blind hatred of Pestis leading her to thoughts like &quot;it's not <i>really </i>evil if I bring down this building to kill Vizier Fever...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-20-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T10:49:33-07:00","id":1313338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1313328#post1313328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I hear there was a bit of a scheduling kerfuffle; they wanted Morticia's arc to be before theirs, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, a pretty good reason immediately presents itself in the form of &quot;Morticia's arcs deal with stuff that touches more of the bigger picture, whereas the Candlelight Brigade always has too many rabbits to chase and wasn't really left wanting for screentime back in Season 2.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if we never met the Wardens of Woe, getting a better look at where Umbra came from shifts her whole placement in the story, especially when you compare it with the shit Chris's arcs have her dealing with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the Tsarina Pestis arc and its...rather mind-screwy antagonists. Nice touch that they called out Sterliza for being just as much of a monster as the Psychos for her blind hatred of Pestis leading her to thoughts like &quot;it's not <i>really </i>evil if I bring down this building to kill Vizier Fever...&quot; </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of little tweaks and nudges to Perdition's background that came up in this arc, but I think the biggest one is just the pointed reminder that (just as the Clockwork Device views Perdition's defection as stemming from a defect) it is a mistake to assume uncritically that the Device \u2014 a distributed entity that we <i>know</i> values its own self-preservation over most any other goal it has \u2014 is little more than a malfunctioning cosmic supercomputer.<br /> <br /> It's easy to forget that the Demiurge is basically the Gnostic Devil. Sometimes it takes a stranger ranting at an empty room to piece that together, and that's delightfully spooky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Misplaced pronoun. 05-20-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T14:58:37-07:00","id":1313386,"title":"","content":"Speaking about the Candlelight Brigade, what do you think about the rumors that they are going to replace one of the core members of the Brigade with a some sort of necromancer/medium girl? While I am interested of seeing her relationship with Morticia, I admit that I was a big fan of AKD, and I think I'll miss him scavenging his basement after the relics of his grandmother and his complicated love/hate relationship with Ranger Stars. Also, I have a weakness for characters with long full name, and Alexander Kostis Dimas is really cool one, IMO. I hope they'll find a way to get him back to the screen in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T16:35:39-07:00","id":1313418,"title":"","content":"(OOC: Now I'm panicking because I could have sworn we had a name for AKD. Be Right Back.)<br /> (EDIT: I have returned with news that Alexander Kostis Dimas is now Totes the canon.)<br /> <br /> I imagine Alex will return down the line-he has good antipathy with Dave, but a lot of people are iffy on if his arc with Christina is over and what his relationship to Amon is going from. I dunno if the writers are concerned with that, but I imagine they're at least thinking out his place in the story.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Morgan Bones is gonna be interesting-I get a vague someone on the staff was a fan of Star Trek TOS with that naming schema, but that asides, the Brigade's approach to darker magics has alwasy been keenly off-beat. Can't wait to see her in action!<br /> <br /> (If I have any spare time tonight, I might glossary the names we have so far in an earlier post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-20-2019, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T02:59:26-07:00","id":1313460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1313418#post1313418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (If I have any spare time tonight, I might glossary the names we have so far in an earlier post)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, when someone is going to make a Wiki for this show? I mean, there are so many minor characters and antagonists in it that it is so complicated to follow all of the subplots even without all the fan names, nicknames and terms. Sheesh.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I must admit I was disappointed that Alex didn't showed up at Candlelight Brigade focused episode for Pestis's arc, as they used the screen time to introduce Morgan officially for the first time. At least he got a cameo, as well as Bianca and her Hellfire Club, even though the latter were more on the side of the Psycho Rangers and Sterliza than the rest of the Brigade (other than Centaur, but they were always known to play both sides for profit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-21-2019, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T07:43:39-07:00","id":1313491,"title":"","content":"I Really like one of Amon\u201ds Antagonist \u201c the One who Paints Landscape\u201d<br /> <br /> Yeah when I heard that name i thought it was really silly to. But man, \u201cGreen is Not a Creative color\u201d has never been so terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T15:16:58-08:00","id":1369916,"title":"","content":"So while the new arc of the Candlelight Brigade is reaching its peak, what do you think of the season so far? While I generally like it, I know that many of the fanbase are somewhat divided by the new plot development, like how Madam Madeleine has decided to withdraw from the Brigade as they never felt comfortable with all of her &quot;spirit medium&quot; attitude, or how Veronica got fired from the police and instead went to open her own private investigator office, not to mention the whole obscure scene where Agent Jones barged into the finale confrontation between Dr. Merrick and his son and now no one is really sure what exactly happened there. Bianca and AKD did showed up more than I expected them to, which makes me really happy as they are two of my favorite characters in the Brigade, even though their positions as main Brigade members was taken by Morgan and Nora, something on which I am still torn about.. Lucita is as amazing as ever, of course.<br /> <br /> Still, I think that the peak is still before us- the Brigade is still tracking down the mysterious slasher, and with Veronica on their side it is only a matter of time before the finale showdown. I think it was hinted that the slasher is much more active than before, and Veronica hinted that there may be more than one, something which would be bad news considering the extremely tense relationships between the Brigade members. They constantly talk about the &quot;incident' without actually saying what happened, but whatever the event was it feels like the Brigade is far less united and stable than before, which means they are also way more vulnerable...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T19:01:24-08:00","id":1369948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1369916#post1369916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while the new arc of the Candlelight Brigade is reaching its peak, what do you think of the season so far?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Renegade Rangers' arc was <i>the</i> <i>shit. </i>I actually dropped the show back in season two, but luckily the new trailer showed up in my recommendations, because that 80s/90s anime look is my jam (also, Mute is best girl).<br /> <br /> I'm going to have to go back and watch the stuff I skipped before I get on with the rest of the season, though. There seem to have some pretty big developments since season 1, like how Morticia's powers work and Amon... being a time traveller now, I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T19:09:01-08:00","id":1369949,"title":"","content":"(Gonna compile that names list tonight)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T20:28:46-08:00","id":1369960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1369948#post1369948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to go back and watch the stuff I skipped before I get on with the rest of the season, though. There seem to have some pretty big developments since season 1, like how Morticia's powers work and Amon... being a time traveller now, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Amon's amnesiac-dreaming-of-past-lives bits from last season got expanded to account for some of the weirder parts of how history works with godlike power \u2014 Stars and Perdition touched on it some time earlier in the current run, and there've been hints that Summer's catching that bug soon, too, but even by those standards, you gotta hand it to Amon for keeping it together.<br /> <br /> Morticia's powers got a bit more\u2026 anchored, for lack of a better term, and they're really leaning into her social life and the back-and-forth she's got with Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T21:09:43-08:00","id":1369963,"title":"","content":"<b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">[WARNING: THE FOLLOWING LIST IS UNDER CONSTRUCTION AND POORLY FORMATTED. THIS IS NOT IT'S FINAL FORM]</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Streaming Sites</u></b><br /> Drive Thru Theatre-Drive Thru RPG<br /> <br /> <b><u>Major Series</u></b><br /> Darkness Rangers-World of Darkness<br /> Darkness Rangers: Neo-Chronicles of Darkness<br /> <br /> <b><u>Main Characters</u></b><br /> Chris/Christina McWolfman/Ranger Moon- Werewolf the Apocalypse(The Garou)/Werewolf the Forsaken(The Forsaken)<br /> Steve Von Mortimer/Ranger Night-Vampire the Masquerade(The Camarilla)/Vampire the Requiem(The Covenants)<br /> Dave Pendragon/Ranger Stars-Mage the Ascension(The Traditions)/Mage the Awakening(The Pentacle Alliance)<br /> Summer Jones/Ranger Dream-Changeling the Dreaming(Kithain)/Changeling the Lost(The Lost)<br /> Morticia Smith/Ranger Eclipse-Wraith the Oblivion/Geist The Sin-Eaters(The Sin-Eaters)<br /> Ranger Void-The Shadow(Wraith)<br /> Ranger Umbra(alternatively Void depending on writer)-The Geist(Geist)<br /> Adam/Ranger Storm-Promethean the Created(The Created)<br /> Amon-Mummy the Resurrection/Mummy the Curse (The Arisen)<br /> Isaac/Ranger Perdition.(Fan Nicknamed Ranger Clockwork)-/Demon the Fallen(The Fallen)/Demon the Descent(The Unchained)<br /> Phoenix &quot;Nyx&quot; Mehta/Ranger Nightmare(Phobos Defender/Ranger Devoured)-Beast the Primordial<br /> The Candlelight Brigade-Hunter the Vigil<br /> <br /> <b><u>Fanfiction</u></b><br /> Brian Eddington-Genius the Transgression<br /> Mira Clea-Princess the Hopeful<br /> Ariel Hendricks-Leviathan the Tempest(???)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Supporting Characters/Sometimes Antagonists</u></b><br /> Mr. Siddhi-The Purified(Immortals)<br /> (unnamed son of Isaac)-The Demon-Blooded(Demon the Descent)<br /> (Chris/tina's unnamed girlfriend)-The Wolf-Blooded(Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Autumn/Legacy-The Autumn Court(Changeling the Lost)<br /> Mother Selena-Luna<br /> Apollo-Helios<br /> Centaur LLC-The Cheiron Group<br /> Dr. Mongol-The Cherion Group? Devaint allusion maybe?<br /> Hell Fire Club-Ashwood Abbey<br /> Lilitu Xangmu-The Dark Mother<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Villains</u></b><br /> Pentax-Pentex(Werewolf the Apocalypse)<br /> The Technocracy-The Technocracy(Mage the Ascension)<br /> Mr. Wyrm-The Wyrm(Werewolf the Apocalypse)<br /> Bloodbath Gang-Blood Bathers(Immortals)<br /> Ranger Paragon-Primordial Heroes(once referenced Mirrors)(Beast the Primordial)<br /> The Ivory Royals, The Ivory Queen, The Ivory Prince, the Ivory Princess-The Ivory Claws(Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Stepmother(specifically, Summer's)-The True Fae(Changeling the Lost)<br /> Namer-The Deceived<br /> Deaf Simon/Rider Conquest-Tyrants(Geist The Sin-Eaters)<br /> Cosmic Device-God-Machine<br /> Birds of Dis/&quot;creepy crows&quot;-Strix<br /> Moon-Banished-Idigam<br /> Wardens of Woe(Reapers, Geist the Sin-Eaters)<br /> Stormchasers(Alchemists, Promethean the Created)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Major Arcs</u></b><br /> Pandora's Box<br /> Children of the Forgotten Stars-Book of the Deceived<br /> Time of Judgement-...Time of Judgement<br /> Imperial-Imperial Mysteries<br /> THe Covenant Pentology(Secrets of the Covenants, Vampire the Requiem)<br /> Tsarina Pestis (The Contagion Chronicle)<br /> Kin of Demeter<br /> <br /> <b><u>Episodes</u></b><br /> The Anti-Smoking Episode-Samuel Haight<br /> The Teen Pregnancy Episode-Forsaken First's &quot;Werewolves shouldn't screw each other thing&quot;, see the Unihar<br /> Long Lost Cousins<br /> The Foolhardy Son<br /> Going South<br /> The Ivory Scarab<br /> <br /> <b><u>In-Universe Terms</u></b><br /> Fathertounge-First Tongue(Spirits, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Iremite-...Iremite(Mummy the Curse)<br /> Divine Speech-High Speech(Mage the Awakening)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Uncertain(Hopefully this List Ceases to Exist)</u></b><br /> Coven of X(Mage the Awakening, but hell if I know who or what they are asides)<br /> Speaker-of-Names(I assume Forsaken again)<br /> Geas of Heaven<br /> Vizier Fever(?)<br /> Mute<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Undealt With List</u></b><br /> Nibbles the Face Jester(Nibbles the Clown, Chronicles of Darkness)<br /> Jersey(Jersey Devil, Chronicles of Darkness)<br /> Dr. Mongol(Progenitor, Deviant the Renegade)<br /> KIB(Kids in Black)(Black-Eyed Kids, Chronicles of Darkness)<br /> Hell Fire Club(Ashwood Abbey, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> Most Dangerous Game Society(THe Hunt Club, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> Cult of the Mad Wolf(The Fire-Touched,Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Mockery Hunter King(The False Father, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Ranger Devoured(Beasts,Beast the Primordial)<br /> Renegade Rangers(Renegades, Deviant the Renegades<br /> Eyeless Devourer(The Blind Man, Beast the Primordial)<br /> Bloody Mother's Chorus(The Circle of the Crone, Vampire the Requeim)<br /> Unknown Tyrant(The Nameless, Vampire the Requiem)<br /> Returned(The Bound, Geist the Sin-Eaters)<br /> Deadlands (The Underworld, Geist the Sin-Eaters)<br /> Stolos Shadows(Strix, Vampire the Requiem)<br /> Lunatic Exiles(Idigam, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Psycho Rangers (Antagonists of the deepest sell-out types)<br /> Psycho Ranger Abyss (Scelesti, Mage the Awakening)<br /> Psycho Ranger Bale (Bale Hounds, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Psycho Ranger Brood (Belial's Brood, Vampire the Requiem)<br /> Morgan Bones(The Council of Bones, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> Alexander Kostis Dimas(Aegis Kai Doru, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> The One Who Paints Landscapes (The Painter, Mummy the Curse)<br /> Madame Madeleine(Les Mysteres)<br /> Veronica(VASCU)<br /> Agent Jones(Valkyrie)<br /> Dr. Merrick (Merrick Instititue)<br /> Nora(SWORN, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> Thief Ali(Wadjet-Itja, Mummy the Curse)<br /> Judge Badria(The Benbenet, Mummy the Curse)<br /> Lords of Justice(The Judges, Mummy the Curse)<br /> Dark Terrors (The Night Horror Series)<br /> Young King(Tyrants, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> The Adopted(Mimics, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> The Guests(Hosts, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Goodlove(Ranger Lovegrove, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Gregory(The Geryo, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Lisa/Ranger Chrysalis(Deviants, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Torment Spider(The Web of Pain, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Dr. Moreau (Progenitors, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Makilu(Dinosaur Magath, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Brother Grimm(Changing Breeds)<br /> The Silver-Haired Father(Silver Wolf, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> The Hunter-King (Wolf, Werewolf the Forsaken)<br /> Lucita(The Lucifuge, Hunter the Vigil)<br /> Sir Cardian the Death Buster(The Empty, Changeling the Lost<br /> Deimos Weavers(The Devoted, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Mark/Ranger Renegade(The Renegades, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Torn and Thorn(Ship name between Cardian and Mark)<br /> Renegade Hearts(Ship name between Cardian and Mark)<br /> Dr. Originatus(Progenitor, Deviant the Renegades)<br /> Amber(Everlasting, Vampire the Requiem)<br /> Bianca (Ashwood Abbey)<br /> Sterliza(The Crucible Initative, Contagion Crossover)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-21-2020, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T21:41:33-08:00","id":1369968,"title":"","content":"&quot;The HSQ of LLC&quot; is &quot;The Holy Shit Quotient of Long Lost Cousins.&quot; Long Lost Cousins is a nonspecific crossover event that, in the fiction of this series, comes in somewhere around the introduction of Ranger Nightmare. It involves the Strix in some capacity (leaning on the &quot;Kindred&quot; angle) and features Steve acting as the mouthpiece for the larger phenomenon through which &quot;vampires is am liars alot&quot; (and, more prosaically, Pancryptia) can be observed as an example.<br /> <br /> Going South is a nonspecific crossover event whose title is riffing on the Winter Court through Summer's involvement and an implied bad time with the Stepmother. The creepy ravens are Strix or hobgoblins of some stripe, drawing more particularly from the imagery of the Unholy and her durance-esque origin story.<br /> <br /> The Phobos Defender and Lilitu Xangmu are &quot;The Begotten and the Dark Mother, but the post was made before the Kickstarter was out.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure a lot of the other stuff on the Uncertain list is just down to Sikla throwing out a bunch of names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T06:43:12-08:00","id":1370044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1369968#post1369968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure a lot of the other stuff on the Uncertain list is just down to Sikla throwing out a bunch of names.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was definitely her posts where I started going &quot;Wait, wut.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T08:45:39-08:00","id":1370062,"title":"","content":"Satchel's right about the Phobos Defender and Liltu. Dr. Mongol was &quot;Deviant Progenitor before the Kickstarter came out.&quot;<br /> <br /> You forgot the Stormchasers (Promethean alchemists) and the Wardens of Woe (Reapers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:10:44-08:00","id":1370133,"title":"","content":"... dangit guys, I have a hard enough time not making my Changelings Kamen Riders as it stands. Now I have this thread making me want to make the premise of this show into an actual durance. XD So many character ideas, so little time to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:48:44-08:00","id":1370139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1369948#post1369948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Renegade Rangers' arc was <i>the</i> <i>shit. </i>I actually dropped the show back in season two, but luckily the new trailer showed up in my recommendations, because that 80s/90s anime look is my jam (also, Mute is best girl).<br /> <br /> I'm going to have to go back and watch the stuff I skipped before I get on with the rest of the season, though. There seem to have some pretty big developments since season 1, like how Morticia's powers work and Amon... being a time traveller now, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also missed Ranger Renegade's arc due to personal reasons, but I did really enjoyed Amon's new arc (even though from what I understand, its rating was relatively low compared to other arcs. The issue with cult arcs, I guess). It really expanded Amon's background, and presented all kinds of new characters and expended others. I really love the Thief Ali, and Judge Badria was terrifying, especially how she was the literal incarnation of one of the Lords of Justice that Amon serves. The Bloodbath Gang also made alliance with Amon, and Mr Siddhi made a cameo- even though I hoped he would have a larger role in the arc.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while the Candlelight Brigade's arc is still running, it seems like after that the series is going to return to the &quot;monster of the week&quot; kind of progress, as no new arc seems to be announced (well, unless you consider the arcs they plan for the reboot of the original series in honor for the 20th anniversary). I must admit that it makes me a bit disappointed, as I really enjoy the story arcs, but it seems that most fans prefer that format better. I will definitely not complain for more Dark Terrors specials, however- the last one involved some of Steve's lost family members returning with vengeance, not to mention other strange things like the cat plague. While she didn't got a lot of screen time, Amber was my favorite in the episode- she is just a great character with so much potential, and besides, the horror on Steve's face when he broke into her museum and discovered her &quot;collection&quot; was priceless. While I doubt she would make a comeback, I do hope the writers would bring her again.<br /> <br /> OOC- yeah, I know Arc that I am making your work more complicated with this post, but the show must go on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:25:34-08:00","id":1370160,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the Uncertain List, the Kin of Demeter story line seems to refer to something in the WoD universe, I assume it is about W:tA because of the name, but I have no idea currently what specifically it refers to. Makilu, on the other hand, is probably a reference for the Mokele from Apocalypse. Silver Haired Father is probably Silver Wolf, but again I'm not sure (could also be Storm Wolf), and yeah, Hunter King is very likely Father Wolf. Not sure about the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:37:09-08:00","id":1370164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1370062#post1370062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel's right about the Phobos Defender and Liltu. Dr. Mongol was &quot;Deviant Progenitor before the Kickstarter came out.&quot;<br /> <br /> You forgot the Stormchasers (Promethean alchemists) and the Wardens of Woe (Reapers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Work in Progress. I made it big and everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T17:54:55-08:00","id":1370197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1370160#post1370160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the Uncertain List, the Kin of Demeter story line seems to refer to something in the WoD universe, I assume it is about W:tA because of the name, but I have no idea currently what specifically it refers to. Makilu, on the other hand, is probably a reference for the Mokele from Apocalypse. Silver Haired Father is probably Silver Wolf, but again I'm not sure (could also be Storm Wolf), and yeah, Hunter King is very likely Father Wolf. Not sure about the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kin of Demeter brings to mind the Children of Gaia, at least to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T16:58:35-07:00","id":1374988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1370139#post1370139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also missed Ranger Renegade's arc due to personal reasons, but I did really enjoyed Amon's new arc (even though from what I understand, its rating was relatively low compared to other arcs. The issue with cult arcs, I guess). It really expanded Amon's background, and presented all kinds of new characters and expended others. I really love the Thief Ali, and Judge Badria was terrifying, especially how she was the literal incarnation of one of the Lords of Justice that Amon serves. The Bloodbath Gang also made alliance with Amon, and Mr Siddhi made a cameo- even though I hoped he would have a larger role in the arc.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while the Candlelight Brigade's arc is still running, it seems like after that the series is going to return to the &quot;monster of the week&quot; kind of progress, as no new arc seems to be announced (well, unless you consider the arcs they plan for the reboot of the original series in honor for the 20th anniversary). I must admit that it makes me a bit disappointed, as I really enjoy the story arcs, but it seems that most fans prefer that format better. I will definitely not complain for more Dark Terrors specials, however- the last one involved some of Steve's lost family members returning with vengeance, not to mention other strange things like the cat plague. While she didn't got a lot of screen time, Amber was my favorite in the episode- she is just a great character with so much potential, and besides, the horror on Steve's face when he broke into her museum and discovered her &quot;collection&quot; was priceless. While I doubt she would make a comeback, I do hope the writers would bring her again.<br /> <br /> OOC- yeah, I know Arc that I am making your work more complicated with this post, but the show must go on!</div> </div> </div> </div>IC: Though, I will say the reveal in the Summer's arc about why Sir Cardian the Death Buster is called that was a really strong scene, and does explain why he hates the Wardens of Woe so much. Certainly puts to bed the theory of there being multiple Rangers Thorn to bed, and really, the reveal his soul is currently in the possession of the Deimos Weavers makes his crush on Mark a fuckton less creepy and clear it's more than just &quot;Torn and Thorn&quot; sounding nice (yes, I like that better than &quot;Renegade Hearts&quot; as a ship name). When he's not being bossed around, he's ultimately another victim of Dr. Originatus, after all.<br /> <br /> (OOC: This makes more sense if you have Oak, Ash, and Thorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-15-2020, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T18:53:12-07:00","id":1375002,"title":"","content":"I'm so behind. I couldn't understand the series after a certain point but I decided to come back with the latest trailer. Holy sheesh is the animation budget higher \u2014 you can tell the scenes where the new powers are kicking in are a labour of love.<br /> <br /> It's interesting seeing that some of the one-time things I brought up in earlier arcs have been retconned. No one's made mention of Brother Grimm or the Makilu since...season two, I think? Season one? It looks like they had some monster of the week vibes that were going to be a plot, but they were either scrapped or I was looking too deep into it. Any suggestions on need-to-see episodes so I can get caught back up with the show?<br /> <br /> -{OOC: The Varg-Ur and Brother Grimm were a nod to the Changing Breeds book of 1e and the Viking werebears and weird not-Uratha called the Vargir. The Makilu was a nod to the dinosaur magath presented in either Werewolf 1e or Hunting Grounds: The Rockies. The Silver Father was a reference to Silver Wolf and the belief in 1e some of the Pure held that he may have had children with Luna.}-<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T21:27:49-07:00","id":1375012,"title":"","content":"No one's talking about that Ranger Moon Night Terrors mini-arc? Well 'mini' that thing was longer than some season 1 arcs. I like how twisted the theme of family in the first act is, even if few of the villains we're actually about blood relations. Young King was a treat to watch and get kicked in the ass, almost to the point of pity. Almost. The 'adoption' episodes were genuinely scary, 'Ranger Moon v2' was just sad, that fight was fucking grueling to watch and I cried at the end.<br /> <br /> The Guests was some of the best irreedeemable villains I've seen in television and the expansion on them was greatly appreciated. It was great how they still was a bunch of sick fucks while still making them more complex. Though, Goodlove made me cheer for him a couple of times. Ride on, Termite-man.<br /> <br /> (OOC: Young King is a ghost wolf Tyrant, adoption is referring to the Mimics. Guests are Hosts, and Goodlove was Ranger Lovegood)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26000,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26000-hamborger","user":"Hamborger","date":". 03-16-2020, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26000-hamborger","name":"Hamborger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T07:31:24-07:00","id":1375079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hamborger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1375012#post1375012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one's talking about that Ranger Moon Night Terrors mini-arc? Well 'mini' that thing was longer than some season 1 arcs. I like how twisted the theme of family in the first act is, even if few of the villains we're actually about blood relations. Young King was a treat to watch and get kicked in the ass, almost to the point of pity. Almost. The 'adoption' episodes were genuinely scary, 'Ranger Moon v2' was just sad, that fight was fucking grueling to watch and I cried at the end.<br /> <br /> The Guests was some of the best irreedeemable villains I've seen in television and the expansion on them was greatly appreciated. It was great how they still was a bunch of sick fucks while still making them more complex. Though, Goodlove made me cheer for him a couple of times. Ride on, Termite-man.<br /> <br /> (OOC: Young King is a ghost wolf Tyrant, adoption is referring to the Mimics. Guests are Hosts, and Goodlove was Ranger Lovegood)</div> </div> </div> </div>And we shouldn't forget about Christina's big brother Gregory showing up and going full flesh horror as he started to destroy everything. While he was first mentioned in Pists's arc, this time he got the spotlight for himself- and seriously, I get why Chris's father sent him to the asylum. He is a murderous monster, no doubt about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T03:59:52-07:00","id":1375250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1375079#post1375079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we shouldn't forget about Christina's big brother Gregory showing up and going full flesh horror as he started to destroy everything. While he was first mentioned in Pists's arc, this time he got the spotlight for himself- and seriously, I get why Chris's father sent him to the asylum. He is a murderous monster, no doubt about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole 'Made This Way' spiel Gregory went on casts a much more... Sinister light on their father. Interestingly, it seems that Greg doesn't care about <i>being </i>a murderous monster, he hates how he's an <i>abandoned</i> murderous monster. He feels betrayed because dad doesn't give orders and put him in basically a prison(WHich by all means is a good idea, but very much a betrayal) He also didn't seem unstable at all, just his 'pets, so much as very direct and uncaring of collateral.<br /> (OOC: Also Pists? Who dat?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26000-hamborger","name":"Hamborger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T04:48:20-07:00","id":1375257,"title":"","content":"OOC- Tsarina Pestis (I misspelled) seems to be a representation of the Contagion in some form, from Lelial's post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T08:43:46-07:00","id":1375284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1375257#post1375257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOC- Tsarina Pestis (I misspelled) seems to be a representation of the Contagion in some form, from Lelial's post</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OOC: Got in in one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:26:42-07:00","id":1396807,"title":"","content":"OOC: Reviving in honor of the series this imaginary one is probably the most like, She-Ra 2018.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Horde Prime and his ship is probably something that doesn't need adaptation to fit a God-Machine archangel or a tech-themed True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T05:16:23-07:00","id":1397063,"title":"","content":"IC: Anyone get kind of a chunni vibe off Lisa/Ranger Chrysalis? I mean, given what Torment Spider and Dr. Moreau did to her, she has every right to be moody, but her &quot;ALL I FEEL IS PAIN&quot; rants seem like a way to get back to the center of attention after she could no longer be the queen bee of the social scene and a little bitter about how Spider tricked her by playing on her need to be loved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T23:43:12-07:00","id":1397461,"title":"","content":"Two things:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm working on the list, I think I should be able to get it done tonight.<br /> <br /> 2) Ranger Nightmare doesn't have a normal name? Phoenix &quot;Nyx&quot; Mehta. Our cast was looking a little white, so she's at least half-Indian now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Clarifciation: it will not be formatted, and probably not properly listed-but it will have all the names and the sources, unless it's in the I Don't Know category after going through the updates.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and with that, all names are inserted into the text. Now to format the fucker.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What'll probably happen is we'll leave the Streaming Sites, Major Series, Fanfiction, Major Arcs, and Episodes list more or less the same, but we'll break up Main Characters, Supporting Characters, Villains, and In-Universe Terms and reallocate them by gamelines.<br /> <br /> EDIT: the forums have tabling tools, <i>yeeeeeessssss</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-19-2020, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T12:37:50-07:00","id":1397558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1397461#post1397461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm working on the list, I think I should be able to get it done tonight.<br /> <br /> 2) Ranger Nightmare doesn't have a normal name? Phoenix &quot;Nyx&quot; Mehta. Our cast was looking a little white, so she's at least half-Indian now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Clarifciation: it will not be formatted, and probably not properly listed-but it will have all the names and the sources, unless it's in the I Don't Know category after going through the updates.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and with that, all names are inserted into the text. Now to format the fucker.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What'll probably happen is we'll leave the Streaming Sites, Major Series, Fanfiction, Major Arcs, and Episodes list more or less the same, but we'll break up Main Characters, Supporting Characters, Villains, and In-Universe Terms and reallocate them by gamelines.<br /> <br /> EDIT: the forums have tabling tools, <i>yeeeeeessssss</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think Nightmare does, so fine by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T13:27:16-07:00","id":1397567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/450685-i-m-super-excited-for-the-new-series-of-darkness-rangers?p=1397558#post1397558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think Nightmare does, so fine by me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Cross check what I have when you can please, and please get me the Oak, Ash, and Thorn correlations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:31:21-07:00","id":1397754,"title":"","content":"OOC- Nora was intended to be SWORN, because for some stupid google based reason I thought it was a common name amon native americans, which does not seem to be the case, so do with it what you want. I also just want to note that among my posts you seem to missed Lucita, which represents Lady Lucifuge/ Lucifuge as whole. Also, yes, Bianca is an example member of the Hellfire Club/ Ashwood Abbey, and Amber represents the Everlasting from Spilled Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:37:03-07:00","id":1397757,"title":"","content":"Okay. The unsorted ones include:<br /> <br /> Sir Cardian is an Empty, a changeling lich; he's torn out his heart and hidden it away to make it so the death of his physical body just seals him in his dreamscape until he can make a new body from the Hedge.<br /> <br /> The Deimos Weavers are agents of Torment Spider in universe, aka Devoted. <br /> <br /> &quot;Torn and Thorn&quot; and &quot;Renegade Hearts&quot; is a ship name for the romantic tension between Sir Cardian and Mark/Ranger Renegade. In an attempt to help with diversity, let's say &quot;Mark&quot; might be an alias.<br /> <br /> Dr. Originatus is a name I forgot I already applied to Torment Spider's Progenitor, but given how there are multiple conspiracies in the Web of Pain, let's make him a rival of Moreau's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 06-20-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T17:51:57-07:00","id":1397863,"title":"","content":"Also, I forgot: Steriliza is a reference to the Crucible Initiative from Contagion Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}